notes.body:
draft-ietf-masque-h3-datagram-11 extends the quic datagram frame as:
```
   HTTP/3 Datagram {
     Quarter Stream ID (i),
     HTTP Datagram Payload (..),
   }
```
@oesh, what's the best approach to extend the http3 dissector to support h3-datatrams?  Unfortunately, packet-quic.c only calls quic_info->app_handle when it dissects streams.  The first approach, I can think of, is to modify the data param of call_dissector_with_data to contain a boolean variable telling whether the call is about a stream or a datagram.  But this approach is probably not backward compatible, and requires to update not just packet-http3.c, but packet-nbt.c and packet-dns.c as well.  Another approach is to introduce a new quic_proto_dissector_datagram_table besides the currently available quic_proto_dissector_table.  What do you think?

(On top of this Merge Request, I was able to add a rudimentary webtransport support to http3.  Thank you.)

